message: "If you use whatsapp-mcp-kit in research or software, please cite it as below."
title: "whatsapp-mcp-kit"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dziatkovskii
    given-names: Anton
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7408-3054"
    affiliation: "Palo Alto AI Research Lab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tonydzi/whatsapp-mcp-kit"
url: "https://github.com/tonydzi/whatsapp-mcp-kit"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  The linking procedure nobody ships for a WhatsApp MCP server. On top of the upstream
  Node/Baileys server @sjawhar/whatsapp-mcp, this kit adds a live self-refreshing QR page
  that keeps the stdio server alive, scrapes the raw QR string out of its log and renders a
  scannable PNG on localhost, plus two production patches (always emit the raw QR string;
  resolve real group names instead of numeric placeholders), a 27-check regression test
  that needs no phone, no network and no installed server, a dated gotchas page, and a
  security page about the ban risk of an unofficial client. Upstream code is not vendored.
keywords:
  - mcp
  - model-context-protocol
  - whatsapp
  - baileys
  - claude-code
  - agent-tooling
